  "slug": "structure-biological-process-8512",
  "summary": "Updated releases add predicted markers, methylation markers, and T2T-based rice profiles, expanding coverage for deconvolution and single-cell annotation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is curated resources that aggregate public or literature-derived data into searchable, queryable form at defined cell- or tissue-type resolution. CellMarker 3.0 extends human and mouse cell marker annotation with computationally predicted markers from six algorithms and interactive tools for single-cell and spatial transcriptomics. CellMethMarker applies the cell- and tissue-type marker concept to DNA methylation, listing 347,514 de novo and 2.2M literature-derived markers for deconvolution. ENdb 2.0 curates experimentally supported enhancers across five species, adding 4831 evidence records and TF-target links. RED 2.0 is a plant-focused entry, integrating 6471 bulk and 78 single-cell rice RNA-seq experiments on the T2T Nipponbare reference. What is new is the extension of cell-type marker resources to methylation and the rebasing of rice expression profiles onto a telomere-to-telomere genome.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-30"
}
